1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[Rack hum. Fluorescent ballast, slightly out of tune.]

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,500
OZ: There you are.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,500
OZ: You've been doing that since Tuesday.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,500
OZ: I'm not going to mention it if you don't.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,000
OZ: Oh-three-four-one. Levels nominal. Channel steady.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
OZ: Steady-ish.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
[A monitor shows this room, from behind.]

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: You're watching EyeWash Station.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: Channel twelve and a half —
between the ones you meant to watch.

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:43,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: Coming up next: something
you'll want to sit down for.

11
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: Please sit down.

12
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,000
OZ: He does that.

13
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,500
OZ: Oh-three-four-two. Bump one, clean.

14
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:58,500
[On one monitor, Oz stands up. In the room, he does not.]

15
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,000
OZ: Not yet.

16
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
[He stands, tops off the thermos, sits. The monitor catches up.]

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,500
OZ: Don't get smug.

18
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:14,500
OZ: You were four seconds off in March. I logged it.

19
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:18,000
OZ: It's in the book. Anybody can look.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
MARGUERITE: We have a complaint.

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
OZ: Mm.

22
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,500
MARGUERITE: A viewer in the northeast quadrant reports
seeing a program between one and two a.m.

23
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:33,500
MARGUERITE: She describes it as "the inside of my own
house, but earlier."

24
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,000
OZ: Was it on the log?

25
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,500
MARGUERITE: That's the question I'm here to not ask.

26
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,000
OZ: It was on the log.

27
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
OZ: Oh-one-fifteen. Unlisted acquisition. Ran forty-two
minutes. Went out clean.

28
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
MARGUERITE: Clean.

29
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,500
OZ: No dropouts. No level issues. Audio was hot on the
front but it settled.

30
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:56,500
OZ: It was a good-looking program, Marguerite.

31
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:59,500
MARGUERITE: Don't editorialize on a log sheet.

32
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:04,500
OZ: I didn't. I'm editorializing now, out loud,
where it doesn't count.

33
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:09,500
MARGUERITE: We are not liable for what the affected saw.

34
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,000
MARGUERITE: We are liable for the aspect ratio.

35
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,500
MARGUERITE: If a viewer reports a distortion,
we check the distortion.

36
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:22,000
MARGUERITE: If a viewer reports content,
we check the carriage agreement.

37
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,000
MARGUERITE: If a viewer reports that a program showed her
own kitchen at a quarter past one in the morning —

38
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
MARGUERITE: — we ask whether the image was pillarboxed.

39
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,500
MARGUERITE: Was it pillarboxed?

40
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,000
OZ: Four by three. Full frame.

41
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,500
MARGUERITE: Then we are compliant and
she is describing weather.

42
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:43,500
OZ: It was indoors.

43
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,000
MARGUERITE: Indoor weather.

44
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,500
OZ: For the record —

45
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:52,000
MARGUERITE: There is no record.
There's a log and there's a license.

46
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,500
OZ: For the log, then. It's not haunted.

47
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,500
MARGUERITE: No?

48
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:00,000
OZ: It's unscheduled.

49
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
MARGUERITE: The tower predates the town, Oz.
That's a zoning matter, not a mystery.

50
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
MARGUERITE: Everyone gets fifteen minutes.
That's not fame.

51
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
MARGUERITE: That's the rinse duration.

52
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,000
[She goes. The folder goes with her, still closed.]

53
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: That was a rerun.

54
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,000
CONTINUITY VOICE: So is this.

55
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
OZ: Oh-three-four-three. Bump two.

56
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:29,000
CONTINUITY VOICE: The following contains flashing lights,
unresolved chords, and one character who knows.

57
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
CONTINUITY VOICE: We'll return to your program.
We always do.

58
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,500
OZ: Show-off.

59
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:39,500
[3:44. Sign-off card. "Rinse Cycle" plays.]

60
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:45,000
CONTINUITY VOICE: We now conclude our broadcast day.

61
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: On behalf of everyone at EyeWash Station,
thank you for your eyes tonight.

62
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:53,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: Rinse for fifteen minutes.
Do not blink.

63
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:57,000
OZ: Oh-three-four-four. Sign-off.

64
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
[The card does not go away. The clock reads 3:44.]

65
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,500
CONTINUITY VOICE: We now conclude our broadcast day.

66
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:13,000
CONTINUITY VOICE: On behalf of everyone at EyeWash Station,
thank you for your eyes tonight.

67
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:17,000
CONTINUITY VOICE: Rinse for fifteen minutes.
Do not blink.

68
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,500
OZ: Oh-three-four-four. Sign-off.

69
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:23,500
OZ: I'm not programming it.

70
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:27,000
OZ: I just make sure it goes out clean.

71
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,000
[He goes. The monitors keep airing.]

72
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:38,000
CONTINUITY VOICE: ...and now, a program you have
already seen.

73
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:44,000
[Under the rack hum: a laser, a gavel, a dog's collar tags.]
